Follow Lipstick's screen rotation at runtime.

Lipstick reports rotation only through the wl_output transform. On wl_output.done
the content rotation (0/90/180/270) is updated, the logical size swapped, and the
buffer kept in the panel's native orientation, with the content drawn
pre-rotated into it. Fullscreen windows use wl_shell plus the Qt surface
extension, as native Silica apps do, so that set_buffer_transform tells Lipstick
the content orientation (edge gestures follow) instead of making it rotate the
buffer back. While shown as an app cover the content is drawn portrait. Maliit
gets appOrientationChanged, and its input-method area (native coordinates) is
mapped into the rotated view for the keyboard inset. The native surface is
resized with un-rotated dimensions.

FLUTTER_SFOS_ROTATION=0 disables rotation. FLUTTER_SFOS_SHELL=xdg keeps
xdg_shell and the upstream behaviour (no runtime rotation).
Vendors surface-extension.xml (BSD, The Qt Company) from sailfishos/qtwayland.

